A `prefix.changed` naming `text` over a diff that moved a tool. The reason must
be the strongest class the diff itself supports, and `PrefixReason`'s
declaration order IS that precedence -- `tools` outranks `text`.

A row that names the wrong class has attributed a miss to the wrong part of the
head, which is worse than not attributing it: the reader stops looking.
`PrefixDelta::reason` is the single statement of which delta supports which
class, and both the writer and this check read it.
